@lang en
IMPORT `uic-par-average-deductible`

-- The exclusions of the UIC Property All Risks wording: A, excluded causes (src:37-180), and
-- B, excluded property (src:183-249). src:N is line N of ../../source/raw/uic-par.txt.
--
-- HOW CAUSATION IS READ (fork F5). Each piece of property carries a causal chain (see the
-- nouns module): the direct cause, the earlier causes that led to it, and other causes that
-- contributed at the same time.
--   * A1 ("gây ra bởi", caused by) and A2 ("gây ra bởi hay phát sinh từ", caused by or arising
--     from) reach the chain: the direct cause and the earlier causes. That A1 reaches earlier
--     causes is shown by its own exceptions, which rescue "subsequent" loss from a later cause
--     and would be idle if only the direct cause counted.
--   * A3 and A4 ("trực tiếp hay gián tiếp", directly or indirectly; "có liên quan đến", in
--     connection with) reach every cause, concurrent ones included; A3(c) says so in terms
--     (src:131-132).
--
-- WHAT "A CAUSE NOT EXCLUDED" MEANS. Three exceptions turn on a "cause not excluded in the
-- Policy" (src:51, 66, 89, 94, 237). It is tested with `a cause the wording excludes, as it
-- acted on`: the cause is on a list of section A, or is one of the B3(f)-(h) and B5 causes,
-- taking the property's own circumstances into account. For an EARLIER loss to other property
-- the earlier loss's circumstances are not in the record, so this property's are used
-- (fork F6).

§ `The exclusions`
-- src:35 | CÁC ĐIỂM LOẠI TRỪ

§§ `The causes that reached the property`

GIVEN `the piece` IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A cause`
`the causes in the chain of` `the piece` MEANS
    `the piece`'s `the direct cause` FOLLOWED BY `the piece`'s `the earlier causes in the chain`

GIVEN `the piece` IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A cause`
`every cause of` `the piece` MEANS
    append (`the causes in the chain of` `the piece`) (`the piece`'s `the other contributing causes`)

GIVEN `the piece`  IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
      `the causes` IS A LIST OF `A cause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the chain of` `the piece` `includes one of` `the causes` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD elem c `the causes`) (`the causes in the chain of` `the piece`)

GIVEN `the piece`  IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
      `the causes` IS A LIST OF `A cause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some cause of` `the piece` `is one of` `the causes` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD elem c `the causes`) (`every cause of` `the piece`)

GIVEN `the piece`        IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
      `the circumstance` IS A `A circumstance of the property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the piece` `was` `the circumstance` MEANS
    elem `the circumstance` (`the piece`'s `its circumstances`)

GIVEN `the piece` IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
      `the kinds` IS A LIST OF `A kind of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the piece` `is of a kind in` `the kinds` MEANS
    any (GIVEN k YIELD elem k `the kinds`) (`the piece`'s `what it is`)

