GIVETH A LIST OF `A cause`
`the unconditional causes in A1(c)` MEANS
    LIST `fraudulent or dishonest acts`,
         `disappearance, unexplained shortage, or shortage found at stocktaking`,
         `misfiling or misplacement of information`,
         `shortage in the supply or distribution of materials`,
         `shortage due to an error in accounting or record-keeping`,
         `cracking, fracture, collapse or overheating of boilers, economisers, vessels or pipes containing liquid or gas`,
         `leakage at joints or failure of welds of boilers`,
         `mechanical or electrical breakdown or derangement of machinery or equipment`

@ref UIC PAR, Exclusion A1(c), src:69-85
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `A cause`
      `the piece` IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cause` `is an A1(c) cause, as it acted on` `the piece` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the cause` EQUALS `theft`
           THEN NOT `the piece` `was` `stolen at a building with force and violence used to enter it or to escape from it`
           IF `the cause` EQUALS `bursting, overflowing, discharge or leakage of water from tanks, apparatus or pipes`
           THEN `the piece` `was` `in a building that was empty or not in use`
           OTHERWISE elem `the cause` `the unconditional causes in A1(c)`

