GIVETH A LIST OF `A cause`
`the unconditional causes in A1(d)` MEANS
    LIST `river or sea erosion`, `subsidence, ground movement or landslip`, `normal settlement of new structures`,
         `freezing or solidification of molten material`, `accidental discharge of molten material`

-- (iv): wind, rain, hail, frost, snow, flood, sand or dust, only where they act on movable
-- property in the open or in a building not enclosed on all sides, or on fences or gates.
-- "Bão tố" (storm), a carve-back peril of Exclusion B1, is not on this list (fork F9).
GIVETH A LIST OF `A cause`
`the weather causes in A1(d)(iv)` MEANS
    LIST `wind`, `rain`, `hail`, `frost`, `snow`, `flood`, `sand or dust`

@ref UIC PAR, Exclusion A1(d), src:97-107
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `A cause`
      `the piece` IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cause` `is an A1(d) cause, as it acted on` `the piece` MEANS
        elem `the cause` `the unconditional causes in A1(d)`
    OR  (    elem `the cause` `the weather causes in A1(d)(iv)`
         AND (   `the piece` `was` `movable property in the open, or in a building not enclosed on all sides`
              OR `the piece` `is of a kind in` (LIST `fences or gates`)))

