§§ `What counts as "a cause not excluded"`

-- Section A's lists, with the conditions of A1(c)(i), A1(c)(vi) and A1(d)(iv), and the causes
-- of B3(f)-(h) and B5 where the property is of the kind those limbs name. Used only by the
-- three exceptions; never as an exclusion in its own right.
GIVETH A LIST OF `A cause`
`the unconditional causes in section A` MEANS
    foldr append EMPTY
        (LIST `the causes in A1(a)(i)`, `the causes in A1(a)(ii)`, `the causes in A1(b)(i)`, `the causes in A1(b)(ii)`,
              `the unconditional causes in A1(c)`, `the unconditional causes in A1(d)`,
              `the causes in A2(a)`, `the causes in A2(b)`,
              `the causes in A3(a)`, `the causes in A3(b)`, `the causes in A3(c)`, `the causes in A3(d)`,
              `the causes in A3(e)`, `the causes in A4`)

@ref UIC PAR, exceptions at src:51-53, 65-67, 89-95 and 236-238; fork F6
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `A cause`
      `the piece` IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cause` `is a cause the wording excludes, as it acted on` `the piece` MEANS
        elem `the cause` `the unconditional causes in section A`
    OR  `the cause` `is an A1(c) cause, as it acted on` `the piece`
    OR  `the cause` `is an A1(d) cause, as it acted on` `the piece`
    OR  elem `the cause` (LIST `a process the property was undergoing`,
                               `work on the property: refurbishing, repair, testing, installation or servicing`)
    OR  (    `the cause` EQUALS `installation, moving or relocation of machinery or equipment, including dismantling and re-erection`
         AND `the piece` `is of a kind in` `machinery and equipment, for Exclusion B3(g)`)
    OR  (    `the cause` EQUALS `explosion or rupture of a boiler, economiser, turbine, or other vessel, machinery or apparatus in which pressure is used`
         AND `the piece` `is of a kind in` (LIST `a boiler, economiser, turbine, or other vessel, machinery or apparatus in which pressure is used, or its contents`))

-- Exception (i) of A1(a), A1(c) and B3(h): "subsequent" Loss from a cause not excluded. The
-- loss to this property is that subsequent loss when the cause that acted on it directly is
-- not excluded; the excluded cause is then earlier in the chain, and only the later loss is
-- paid ("chỉ chịu trách nhiệm đối với các Tổn thất phát sinh sau đó").
@ref UIC PAR, src:51-53, 89-91, 236-238
GIVEN `the piece` IS A `A piece of property lost or damaged`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`exception (i), subsequent Loss from a cause not excluded, holds for` `the piece` MEANS
    NOT `the piece`'s `the direct cause` `is a cause the wording excludes, as it acted on` `the piece`

